# VANISHING TWIN SYNDROME

```
One yolk, two heartbeats,
then one flattening against
church chamber wall.

He orbits her into
no orbit at all.
Blue-red moon that quit turning.

She marrows into him, lithopedion,
a stone child carried for years
inside the twin
who practiced Eucharist.

Castor drowns
in the crook of an elbow.
Pollux begs the dark splitting
his ration of forever,
finds it already gone.

One placenta. Two mouths
mouthing the same source dry.

At night they star each other
into a single point —
astronomers still log
two lights, though only one
still burns.

Under her ribs, a papery weight
that used to answer
to a name.

Her hand goes numb
from holding,
what will she not put down?
```

